    "result_text": "All tests green. The full suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test class \u2014 `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature following the existing derived-field conventions in this evolved Spring PetClinic.\n\n**Input field (`title`)** \u2014 accepts `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`, optional:\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `title` to the `OwnerFields` schema (string, `pattern: ^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$`), so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` carry it and Bean Validation rejects bad values.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the persisted `title` column with getter/setter and the same `@Pattern` constraint.\n- Added `title VARCHAR(3)`/`TEXT` to all four schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`); the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column was required.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner` \u2014 carries `title` through the manual field copy.\n\n**Derived field (`salutation`)** \u2014 read-only on the response:\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema.\n- `Owner.salutation(title, lastName)` \u2014 static helper returning `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given (matches the single-source-of-truth derivation style used by the other computed fields).\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 added the `salutation` mapping expression plus a `formatSalutation` default method, mirroring `displayName`/`initials`.\n\n`title` maps by name in both directions automatically; `salutation` is composed in the mapper. The acceptance test (`title=\"DR\"`, `lastName=\"who\"` \u2192 `salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes.",
